{"title":"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Crossnumber Puzzle","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Puzzle\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Puzzle</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Clues\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Clues</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Across\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Across</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Down\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Down</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Puzzle\">Puzzle</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Puzzle\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Below is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> puzzle grid with each square either white or black. Each of the black squares is marked with the letter B. Twenty-eight of the white squares are marked with the numbers 1 through 28.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Clues\">Clues</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Clues\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Across\">Across</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Across\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>2. A number whose digits sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.<br />\n4. A multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6626a2380ff72f6b03fa209d3e479609bd61a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"95\" height=\"25\" />.<br />\n6. The area of a triangle with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/acea4caa250c27e9bf8754443246d59d84e65cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{3 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2e3283226fd22ff84585e358b36900f54d5143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{25 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"91\" height=\"25\" />.<br />\n8. A number that is the product of two equal integers.<br />\n10. The mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/2/5925d480f3806997b54852da751aedca6cfc801b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb55ec21f9b0dcb776bd40b513b12ef2392f22f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{18 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />.<br />\n12. The number of years in a decade.<br />\n13. A number whose tens digit is the mean of its other two digits.<br />\n15. A number that is the same when the digits are written in reverse order.<br />\n16. The product of three consecutive integers.<br />\n18. The sum of the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, inclusive.<br />\n20. A factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f9fbb7b5540a8d2356d1d87913ea8e0eeb15e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{17 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"91\" height=\"25\" />.<br />\n22. The smallest whole number that is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2e3283226fd22ff84585e358b36900f54d5143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{25 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"91\" height=\"25\" />.<br />\n24. The perimeter of a triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.<br />\n25. The positive difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4db801f17f083699a1a8ddae5731d1d012b0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$987$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815c3c71386b6a6a5d2b338754331461641cc8d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$234$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.<br />\n27. A number whose digits are three consecutive integers, in some order.<br />\n28. A prime number.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Down\">Down</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Down\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>1. The area of a rectangle with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f43631dc3730b2f924b79a2680d958191c5d13b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{24 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" /> and width <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/acea4caa250c27e9bf8754443246d59d84e65cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{3 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" />.<br />\n3. The largest number that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249f6c7d94f60f07968395ca19214325629974d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$165$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> are divisible by.<br />\n4. A multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.<br />\n5. A number whose digits multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.<br />\n7. A number whose digits are the same as the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e93505900865239b282fe30bb289bb1ec51abcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{27 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />, but not necessarily in the same order.<br />\n9. A number that lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d21951603a6e6a8118d5f3a6d64f769437f0768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/780b4cd0de492e13118edb30244e2266ffadd1cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4035$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> on the number line.<br />\n11. The number of apple fritters in a box containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dozen.<br />\n13. The mean of the three digits in this number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.<br />\n14. This number appears in the sequence where the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and each term after the first is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f43631dc3730b2f924b79a2680d958191c5d13b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{24 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" /> more than the previous term.<br />\n15. The result when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72e0650e583a8844130183d7430bf808ea6ca67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"95\" height=\"25\" /> is multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/acea4caa250c27e9bf8754443246d59d84e65cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{3 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" /> and then added to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.<br />\n17. The number that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/ead3b7508463cec715e65e4ca4c73f4675bd185a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$462$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.<br />\n19. The mode of the three digits of this number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.<br />\n21. The sum of the digits of this number is equal to the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92ee848b9f6136621805127d03e2c6810bf108bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{15 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />.<br />\n23. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/774551ddb5fe2cc41155715df71ef0c57318f313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 + \\boxed{6 \\text{ ACROSS}} - 1.5 \\times 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"221\" height=\"25\" />.<br />\n25. The number of quarters (worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbcfc22da43fe3886c3ff0069a4ade504c70d307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> each) needed to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/2128551623a1a567a5c0c30f58ad1eafbe0de604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$19.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />.<br />\n26. The positive difference between the two digits of this number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \nWe can find many of the different answers without knowing the other answers first:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1eed7354ac20840b06d6885de96f9a467adccbae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{12 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />: In a decade, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd7ae6c302dec5c5be789f3d4d9be37d000d0772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> years.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb55ec21f9b0dcb776bd40b513b12ef2392f22f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{18 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />: The sum of the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the sum of the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minus the sum of the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fdec521583cd85a3334ce89a7f474f377ba7a443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{19 \\times 20}{2} - \\frac{10 \\times 11}{2} = 190 - 55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"241\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1a13a2b234b06ae55716856e0c89382c3840284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{135}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f43631dc3730b2f924b79a2680d958191c5d13b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{24 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />: The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of its three side lengths, which would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3d71c4eaa44f0e4beae64cb651f022227287200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 + 21 + 25 = 34 + 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"184\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/542094e735da397edc374f3ee342a22f5426ca0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{59}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a10e159c94ece3bb9c55305b6baf831b0ea648e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{25 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />: The larger number of the two is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4db801f17f083699a1a8ddae5731d1d012b0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$987$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and the smaller number of the two is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/5/815c3c71386b6a6a5d2b338754331461641cc8d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$234$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, so the positive difference between the two is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e00a630b73c2983c26b49f34d20e68b0af30ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$987 - 234 = \\boxed{753}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/07894f0d065551929bf1bb3cea58ec30bfddab77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{3 \\text { DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" />: We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97e4c9247c71781675651acee57b3ed350c939b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 = 3 \\times 40 = 2^{3} \\times 3 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"206\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095e93e746013a9e7ba9b2fbe10f0b3f0824f401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$165 = 11 \\times 15 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"217\" height=\"15\" />. Using these prime factorizations, we see that the GCD of the two numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7d97a268ef531e75d99b8a87b8126cdfc0cb06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 5 = \\boxed{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af94355887904453689cb6be192e053e90ba8bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{11 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"91\" height=\"25\" />: Each dozen would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> apple fritters, and each box has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dozens. Thus, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/6/b16eb9c5de3648adebfd2188441106fc4af08426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times 11 = \\boxed{132}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" /> apple fritters.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f9fbb7b5540a8d2356d1d87913ea8e0eeb15e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{17 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"91\" height=\"25\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of a number is just half of that number, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/ead3b7508463cec715e65e4ca4c73f4675bd185a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$462$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015ae10d3bdf0c98d61dd0cd096aee4b9aa52d5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{462}{2} = \\boxed{231}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d2e3283226fd22ff84585e358b36900f54d5143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{25 \\text{ DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"91\" height=\"25\" />: Since each quarter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbcfc22da43fe3886c3ff0069a4ade504c70d307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and the total value of all the quarters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/2128551623a1a567a5c0c30f58ad1eafbe0de604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$19.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, the number of quarters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd54a47c89097e909eb715e2a544425235166723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\$19.50}{\\$0.25} = \\boxed{78}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"110\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Next, we can fill out some more boxes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6626a2380ff72f6b03fa209d3e479609bd61a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"95\" height=\"25\" />: The sum of the digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the tens digit would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32be258d1b99e35f20f3d67b19d8e9bcd4267c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 - 1 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. This means that the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3fadaa111eea58b1835644c54d879949bfa94f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{71}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab087ecb9346424c6e2c35d6d9d96bb66cf4018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{6 \\text{ ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"95\" height=\"25\" />: The base of the triangle would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the height would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d15d808807bfa561e72dc8111649ed0a204ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that the area of the triangle would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5f7135d165818a5b1cddada763c5100d0f806bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 15 \\times 78 = 39 \\times 15 = \\boxed{585}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"241\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4be8478edfe82ae5106a6a125dd16d2432746987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{22 \\text{ACROSS}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"98\" height=\"25\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71e1d81e9d43f49171477ca6e8a8f996ddda7d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 = 2^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c61b19089f2a0c78377d7fc6ac37bc3cd85be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78 = 39 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e058d401a1b942f106f081ff1fcca8a8b1d42a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the least common multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d15d808807bfa561e72dc8111649ed0a204ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2e31de9510c906d1e1f3c321bfb27c31214b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$39 \\times 2^{3} = 39 \\times 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade1746cfb81a064e679b90ec858f103e8ff0d80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{312}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32503dd220d977ee4378d4b730712855eb0beff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1 \\text { DOWN}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"82\" height=\"25\" />: The length of the rectangle would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe61e5b80572ad5a200a0d9cd354ce12a8c7800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the width would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The area of a rectangle is equal to its length multiplied by its width, so the area would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895d0a2b45b2241c9fbe75637dd1cb2044c50f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$59 \\times 15 = \\boxed{885}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC\">2025 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Logic_Puzzle\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Logic Puzzle\">Logic Puzzle</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Crossnumber Puzzle</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Logic_Puzzle\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Logic Puzzle\">Logic Puzzle</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 1\">Practice Relay 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 2\">Practice Relay 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 3\">Practice Relay 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Practice_Relay_Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Practice Relay Problem 4\">Practice Relay 4</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 1\">Relay A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 2\">Relay A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 3\">Relay A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Relay A 4</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1\">Relay B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 2\">Relay B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 3\">Relay B 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 4\">Relay B 4</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 1\">Relay C 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 2\">Relay C 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Relay C 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_C_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay C Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Relay C 4</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Team_Up_Challenge\" title=\"CEMC Team Up Challenge\">CEMC Team Up Challenge</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017142911\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.065 seconds\nReal time usage: 2.083 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 461/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 4390/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 244/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17879/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00% 2046.308      1 -total\n  0.36%    7.400      1 Template:CEMC_TUC_box\n  0.27%    5.424      1 Template:Solution\n  0.26%    5.400      3 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37475:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017142909 and revision id 293856. Rendering was triggered because: page-edit\n -->\n</div>"}